{
  "topic": "How fish gills work",
  "language": "en",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "How do fish breathe? 🐟",
  "hook": "How do fish breathe underwater, when almost none of them have lungs?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_hook",
      "narration": "How do fish breathe underwater, when almost none of them have lungs?",
      "on_screen_text": "How do fish breathe?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "fish"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_oxygen",
      "narration": "Water has dissolved oxygen, but very little: about thirty times less than air.",
      "on_screen_text": "Very little oxygen",
      "highlight_words": [
        "oxygen"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_mouth",
      "narration": "The fish takes water in through its mouth and pushes it out the sides, across its gills.",
      "on_screen_text": "Mouth → gills",
      "highlight_words": [
        "gills"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_gills",
      "narration": "Gills are arches with hundreds of red filaments packed with blood vessels.",
      "on_screen_text": "The gills",
      "highlight_words": [
        "gills"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_lamellae",
      "narration": "Each filament has ultra-thin plates where oxygen passes from the water into the blood.",
      "on_screen_text": "Ultra-thin plates",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Ultra-thin"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_counter",
      "narration": "The trick: blood flows the opposite way to the water, so they can pull out up to eighty percent of the oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "Countercurrent flow",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Countercurrent"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_co2",
      "narration": "And at the same time, they release carbon dioxide into the water.",
      "on_screen_text": "CO₂ goes out",
      "highlight_words": [
        "CO₂"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_air",
      "narration": "Out of the water, the gills collapse and stop working, which is why a fish suffocates in air.",
      "on_screen_text": "They suffocate in air",
      "highlight_words": [
        "suffocate"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_shark",
      "narration": "And some sharks, like the great white, must keep swimming so water flows over their gills.",
      "on_screen_text": "Swim to breathe",
      "highlight_words": [
        "breathe"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "pez_outro",
      "narration": "Send this to someone with a fish tank.",
      "on_screen_text": "For the fish-tank owner",
      "highlight_words": [
        "fish-tank"
      ],
