  "description": "Water holds far less oxygen than air. Fish take water in through the mouth and push it out over the gills, whose filaments have ultra-thin plates where oxygen passes into the blood; because blood flows opposite to the water, they extract much of the oxygen while releasing CO₂. Out of water the gills collapse, and some sharks must keep swimming to breathe. Original 3D animation.",
